course: dictionary
lesson: 1595
title: Using a checklist
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A checklist is a list of things to do or to bring. You mark each thing when it is done, so you can see what is still left. A checklist helps you not to forget anything.
explain: «That night Dad helps her write a checklist (PE kit, reading book, inhaler, charger).» The brackets show what is on the list. Each thing is a short item, and each one gets a tick when it goes in the bag.
explain: Checklists are useful when there is a lot to remember. «A checklist and a travel bag help children stop leaving things at the other home.» When every item is checked, you know you have everything.
fact: A checklist is a list of things to do or to bring, with a mark beside each one when it is done.
fact: A checklist helps you not to forget anything.
fact: Checklists can be for school, such as a writing checklist with capital letters and full stops.
fact: Checklists can help with maths. If a checklist has 12 tasks and 5 are done, then 12 − 5 = 7 are still to do.
fact: Pilots and doctors use checklists to stay safe, because a checklist makes sure no step is missed.
exercise: «That night Dad helps her write a checklist (PE kit, reading book, inhaler, charger).» How many things are on this checklist? | *4 | 6 | 3 | 5
exercise: Why does a checklist help you? | It makes your bag heavier | *It helps you not to forget anything | It is only for pilots and doctors | It shows you what the weather will be
exercise: Maya has 12 tasks on her checklist and has done 5 of them. How many are still to do? | 5 | 6 | *7 | 17
test: Which item would be useful on a writing checklist? | A pet fish | The weather in June | Your favourite film | *Capital letters and full stops
test: Ruby ticks each item on her packing list as she puts it in her bag. Why does she do this? | *To show it is done and not forgotten | To show she has lost the bag | To say the list is wrong | To make the list longer
exam: Which sentence best explains what a checklist is? | A long story about a trip to the seaside | A kind of phone used to send messages | A picture of a bag full of clothes | *A list of things to do or bring, with a mark when each one is done
